---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Change a board's cover or note; one of --cover, --note and --note-template is needed.
--cover reset returns to the automatic preview, drawn by holst.
--note replaces the note, --note-format markdown reads headings, lists, checkboxes, links and marks from it; --note-template starts it from a built-in note.

USAGE
  holst board edit <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to change

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws         Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --cover file           The cover: a picture file, or reset for the automatic preview
      --note text            The new note, replacing the old: text, @file to read a file, - for stdin
      --note-format format   How the note is written: plain, or markdown; plain by default
      --note-template name   Start the note from a built-in one: todo, agenda, summary, workshop, annotation
  -n, --dry-run              Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b edit "Roadmap" --cover cover.png
  $ holst b edit "Roadmap" --cover reset -n
  $ holst b edit "Roadmap" --note @note.md --note-format markdown
  $ holst b edit "Roadmap" --note-template agenda

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
